# Cloudflare Pages special-cases "404.html" as a redirect target (it
# triggers Cloudflare's own built-in not-found redirect instead of
# serving the file). The form handler also can't be named "form.html":
# Cloudflare's automatic clean-URL canonicalization treats form.html as
# the canonical asset for the route /form and issues its own 308 to
# collapse any /form/<slug> request down to bare /form BEFORE this rule
# gets a chance to run — the exact bug this file's naming works around.
# So it lives at form-render.html (content identical to 404.html) and
# gets rewritten in place at 200, keeping the real slug in the URL bar.
/form/*  /form-render.html  200
